Introduction
Cheyenne, Wyoming, is the state's most populous municipality and is well positioned for continued
economic growth and stability due to our geographic location, physical infrastructure, diverse industry
base, land use vision, and sustainability and inclusiveness values.  Cheyenne is located directly north of
Colorado and is well connected to the State of Wyoming through highways, interstates, and railroads,
making Cheyenne an attractive location for residents and industry.  Our diverse industry base is served
